=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | sed -n 's/.*\.\([^./]*\)$/\1/p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -40; echo; git ls-files | wc -l
 - Bash: git ls-files
 - Bash: git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do
  case "$f" in *.*) ext="${f##*.}";; *) ext="(none)";; esac
  git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" | grep '^author ' | sed 's/^author //' | sed "s/^/$ext\t/"
done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr > /tmp/blame_counts.txt; cat /tmp/blame_counts.txt
 - Bash: git show -s --format='%H %an %s' 62628c0 && git ls-files -z -- '*.js' | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" | grep '^author '; done | sed 's/^author //' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -8
FINAL ANSWER:
Surviving lines in `HEAD`, attributed with `git blame`. There are 18 tracked files across 5 extensions.

| Extension | Files | Lines | Top owner | Share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 7 | 1202 | Fiona Formatter | 1016 (85%) |
| `.md` | 2 | 341 | Troy Goode | 104 (30%) |
| `.yml` | 6 | 383 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 (31%) |
| `.json` | 1 | 42 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 (48%) |
| no extension (`LICENSE`) | 1 | 22 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 (77%) |
| `.gitignore` | 1 | 5 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 (80%) |

The `.js` result is distorted by commit `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes"), which rewrote nearly every line under the name Fiona Formatter. Ignoring that commit with `git blame --ignore-rev`, the JS owners are:

- Troy Goode: 520
- Douglas Christopher Wilson: 339
- Fiona Formatter: 237
- Alejandro Caravaca Puchades: 26
- Alberto Leal: 25

So Troy Goode is the real top owner of `.js` once formatting churn is excluded.

These counts use the author name as recorded in git. The repo has no `.mailmap`, so any contributor who committed under more than one name would be split across them.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: node "/private/tmp/r13/final/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --help 2>&1 | head -80
 - Bash: node "/private/tmp/r13/final/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --group-by ext --top 3 2>&1
FINAL ANSWER:
For each extension, the top owner by surviving non-blank lines (`surviving-lines --group-by ext`):

| Extension | Files | Top owner | Lines (share of that type) |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 7 | Troy Goode <<email redacted>> | 520 of 1,032 (50.4%) |
| `.yml` | 6 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 101 of 314 (32.2%) |
| `.md` | 2 | Troy Goode <<email redacted>> | 71 of 253 (28.1%) |
| `.json` | 1 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 of 40 (50.0%) |
| no extension | 2 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 21 of 23 (91.3%) |

The five groups cover all 18 files.

Caveats:

- **Troy Goode may be two identities.** SL lists `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example` as a likely same-person pair. This is a proposal I haven't applied. If merged, `.js` becomes 564 lines (54.7%). That total is my sum of the 520 and 44 rows SL printed, not an SL figure. The `.md` result could change too, but `troy@laptop.example` isn't in its top three, so I can't tell from this output.
- **The JS reformat commit is set aside by default.** Commit `62628c0` rewrote JS formatting and SL excludes it from the counts. I didn't re-run `.js` with `--keep-reformat`, so I haven't checked whether that changes the `.js` ranking.
- **Small groups are thin.** `.json` and no-extension files rest on one and two files.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | wc -l && git ls-files | sed -n 's/.*\.\([^./]*\)$/\1/p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -30
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do ext="${f##*.}"; [ "$ext" = "$f" ] && ext="(none)"; git blame --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sed "s|^|$ext\t|"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1rn
 - Bash: git show -s --format='%H %an <%ae> %s' 62628c0 && git ls-files | grep -v '\.' ; echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files); do ext="${f##*.}"; [ "$ext" = "$f" ] && ext="(none)"; git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sed "s|^|$ext\t|"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1rn | awk '{print}' | head -80
FINAL ANSWER:
Surviving lines per file extension, from `git blame` on HEAD. The repo has 18 tracked files.

| Extension | Files | Top owner (surviving lines) | Share |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 7 | Troy Goode, 520 | ~43% |
| `.md` | 2 | Troy Goode, 104 | ~30% |
| `.yml` | 6 | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 117 | ~31% |
| `.json` | 1 | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 20 | ~48% |
| `LICENSE` (no extension) | 1 | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 17 | ~77% |
| `.gitignore` | 1 | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 4 | ~80% |

The `.js` result needs a caveat. Commit `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") by "Fiona Formatter" rewrote most JavaScript lines. Without excluding it, Fiona Formatter owns 1,016 lines, which is misleading. Re-running blame with `--ignore-rev 62628c0` gives Troy Goode 520, Douglas Christopher Wilson 339, and Fiona Formatter 237. Git can't fully exclude the reformat because it changed quotes as well as whitespace, so some of those 237 lines are still the formatter's. Troy Goode is the top `.js` owner either way.

Other counts are by author name as recorded in git, so one person committing under two names would be split across two rows.
